# SCG Platform — Task List

## CLI Limitations (to be solved by platform)

These are known limitations of the open-source CLI that the platform resolves:

- **Ephemeral signing keys**: Each `scg init` generates a new ed25519 keypair. No chain of trust across lockfile versions. Platform provides persistent signing with OIDC + JWKS verification.
- **Graph query sanity**: If DSM Bootstrap partially fails, scope/audit Cypher queries may return empty results without error. Platform validates graph state after population.
- **30 embedded profiles**: Only covers top GitHub Actions. Platform provides thousands of curated, continuously updated profiles.
- **Go/Helm ecosystems**: No resolver implemented. Platform adds Go module + Helm chart resolution.
- **No audit logging**: No tamper-evident record of what was checked, when, by whom. Platform logs all operations.

## Phase 3: Platform MVP (Weeks 5-6)

### Infrastructure
- [ ] Platform daemon binary (cmd/scgd/main.go)
- [ ] TieredStore configuration for platform scale
  - Reference shards: Tool, Profile, SecretPattern (always hot)
  - Event shards: Digest, Resolution, Scan, Violation (time-windowed)
- [ ] Database schema for user accounts + subscriptions
- [ ] API key generation and validation
- [ ] Rate limiting per API key tier

### Continuous Resolution Engine
- [ ] Cron job: resolve all known tools on schedule (every 15 min for critical, hourly for others)
- [ ] Drift event detection: when resolution changes, create Violation node
- [ ] Alert pipeline: webhook, email, Slack notifications on drift
- [ ] Resolution queue: prioritize tools with recent changes
- [ ] GitHub webhook listener: detect tag force-pushes in real-time

### REST API
- [ ] `GET /v1/resolve/{ecosystem}/{reference}` — pre-computed resolution
- [ ] `GET /v1/profile/{ecosystem}/{reference}` — security profile
- [ ] `GET /v1/history/{ecosystem}/{reference}` — temporal resolution history
- [ ] `POST /v1/check` — batch validation (lockfile upload)
- [ ] `GET /v1/audit/{repo}` — full audit for a repository
- [ ] `GET /v1/status` — platform health + coverage stats
- [ ] API versioning and deprecation policy

### CLI Integration
- [ ] `resolver/platform.go` — implement platform resolver (SCG_API_KEY)
- [ ] `dsm/client.go` — implement platform profile fetcher
- [ ] Graceful fallback: if platform unavailable, fall back to local resolution
- [ ] Cache platform responses locally (5-minute TTL)

### Subscription Management
- [ ] Stripe integration for billing
- [ ] Free tier: unlimited local scans, no platform access
- [ ] Pro tier ($15-25/mo per org): platform API, pre-resolved hashes, full profiles, alerts, 90-day history
- [ ] Enterprise tier (custom): self-hosted, custom policies, SSO/RBAC, SLA

## Phase 4: DSM Registry (Month 2+)

### Community Profiles
- [ ] `POST /v1/profiles` — community profile submission
- [ ] Review workflow: submit → review → approve → publish
- [ ] Profile versioning with temporal validity
- [ ] GPG signing of approved profiles
- [ ] Automated profile generation via static analysis
- [ ] Profile quality scoring (coverage, accuracy, freshness)

### Web Dashboard
- [ ] Repository overview: all dependencies, risk tiers, drift status
- [ ] Temporal timeline: resolution history visualization
- [ ] Secret exposure map: which steps see which secrets
- [ ] Blast radius viewer: DEPTH expansion from compromised tool
- [ ] Alert management: configure notifications, review history
- [ ] Organization settings: custom policies, team access

### Advanced Features
- [ ] Tyla integration: declarative security policies as rules
  ```prolog
  @source(tool, "graph/nodes", "Tool", ["reference", "ecosystem"]).
  @source(resolves, "graph/edges", "RESOLVES_TO", []).
  at_risk(T) :- resolves(T, D1), resolves(T, D2), D1 \= D2.
  at_risk(T) :- depends(T, Dep), at_risk(Dep).
  ```
- [ ] Custom Tyla policy upload per organization
- [ ] Transitive dependency analysis via variable-length paths
- [ ] CVE correlation: match known vulnerabilities against dependency graph
- [ ] GitHub Advisory Database integration
- [ ] Sigstore/Rekor transparency log integration (keyless signing)

### Scale
- [ ] Multi-region deployment
- [ ] CDN for profile distribution
- [ ] Background workers for resolution (separate from API)
- [ ] Monitoring: Prometheus metrics, Grafana dashboards
- [ ] SLA targets: 99.9% API uptime, <200ms p95 latency

